  "question": {
    "text": "For a periodic motion represented by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sin&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math> the amplitude of the motion is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given the equation of motion is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sin&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Simplify equation (1) to obtain the standard form:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cos</mi><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>&#960;</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>4</mn></mstyle></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Comparing equation (2) with standard equation of&nbsp;SHM&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get amplitude of the given oscillation as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
